===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[play]] (a [[chord]]) as an arpeggio; to play (a piece of music) with arpeggios.
#: {{syn|en|arpeggiate}}
#* '''1819''', {{w|Abraham Rees}} (ed.), ''{{w|Rees's Cyclopædia|The Cyclopædia}},'' London: Longman, Hurst, Rees, Orme & Brown, Volume{{nbsp}}14, entry “Fingering on Keyed Instruments,”<sup>[https://archive.org/details/cyclopaediaoruni14rees/page/n451/mode/1up?q=arpeggioing]</sup>
#*: In practising quick passages, the fingers should be lifted up with a spring, and not allowed to hang on the keys, till wanted again, unless in '''arpeggioing''' chords, or in passages of expression.
#* '''1872''', {{w|Samuel Butler (novelist)|Samuel Butler}}, ''{{w|Erewhon}},'' London: Trübner, Chapter{{nbsp}}4, p.{{nbsp}}29,<sup>[https://archive.org/details/erewhonoroverran00butlrich/page/29/mode/1up?q=arpeggioed]</sup>
#*: {{...}} I could see a man with his head buried forward towards a key-board, and his body swaying from side to side amid the storm of huge '''arpeggioed''' harmonies that came crashing overhead and round.
#* '''1902''', {{w|Booth Tarkington}}, ''The Two Vanrevels,'' New York: McClure, Phillips, Chapter{{nbsp}}1, p.{{nbsp}}11,<sup>[https://archive.org/details/twovanrevels00cogoog/page/n30/mode/1up?q=arpeggioed]</sup>
#*: {{...}} having finished her piano-forte practice, touched her harp twice, and '''arpeggioed''' the Spanish Fandango on her guitar, Miss Betty read two paragraphs of “Gilbert” {{...}}
#* '''1990''', Marcel Montecino, ''Big Time,'' New York: William Morrow, Book{{nbsp}}3, p.{{nbsp}}197,<sup>[https://archive.org/details/bigtime00mont/page/197/mode/1up?q=arpeggioed]</sup>
#*: When his fingers touched the piano, he formed a D7 chord, '''arpeggioed''' it up the inversions, then started singing and playing the “Happy Birthday” song.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To produce arpeggios; to produce sounds resembling arpeggios.
#* '''1898''', {{w|Edward Noyes Westcott}}, ''{{w|David Harum}},'' New York: Grosset & Dunlap, Chapter{{nbsp}}37, p.{{nbsp}}314,<sup>[https://archive.org/details/cu31924022210342/page/n331/mode/1up?q=arpeggioing]</sup>
#*: Herr Schlitz seated himself on the piano chair, pushed it a little back, drew it a little forward to the original place, looked under the piano at the pedals, took out his handkerchief and wiped his face and hands, and after '''arpeggioing''' up and down the keyboard, swung into a waltz of {{w|Frédéric Chopin|Chopin}}’s {{...}}
#* '''1909''', {{w|O. Henry}}, “Whistling Dick’s Christmas Stocking” in ''{{w|Roads of Destiny (short story collection)|Roads of Destiny}},'' Garden City, NY: Doubleday, p.{{nbsp}}357,<sup>[https://archive.org/details/roadsofdestiny0000henr_n4z4/page/357/mode/1up?q=arpeggioed]</sup>
#*: The soaring sound [of the whistling] rippled and trilled and '''arpeggioed''' as the songs of wild birds do not;
#* '''2012''', {{w|Roshi Fernando}}, “At the Barn Dance” in ''Homesick,'' New York: Vintage, p.{{nbsp}}166,<sup>[https://archive.org/details/homesick0000fern/page/166/mode/1up?q=arpeggioed]</sup>
#*: The accordion player '''arpeggioed''' through a chord {{...}}
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive|figurative}} To move (the hand or fingers) against a surface as if playing arpeggios on a keyboard; to touch different points in [[succession]] along a surface.
#* '''1931''', {{w|Kate O'Brien (novelist)|Kate O’Brien}}, ''Without My Cloak,'' London: Penguin, 1987, Book{{nbsp}}2, Chapter{{nbsp}}8, p.{{nbsp}}187,<sup>[https://archive.org/details/withoutmycloak0000obri_f2c6/page/187/mode/1up?q=arpeggioing]</sup>
#*: Her hand was still '''arpeggioing''' softly on his arm.
#* '''1966''', Richard Lancaster, ''Piegan: A Look from Within at the Life, Times, and Legacy of an American Indian Tribe,'' Garden City, NY: Doubleday, p.{{nbsp}}168,<sup>[https://archive.org/details/pieganlookfromwi0000lanc/page/168/mode/1up?q=arpeggioed]</sup>
#*: the prickle of [[horripilation]] which '''arpeggioed''' my spine as I came barrelling down the hill from that ghost house
#* '''2009''', {{w|Kevin Crossley-Holland}}, ''The Hidden Roads,'' London: Quercus, p.{{nbsp}}136,<sup>[https://archive.org/details/hiddenroadsmemoi00cros/page/136/mode/1up?q=arpeggioed]</sup>
#*: While we thanked him for having us and told him the car was packed, and so on, he '''arpeggioed''' his stumpy fingers across his scarlet blanket.

